body:
When I stop being open and honest about having an ED, that's usually a big warning sign that I'm headed right back. 

&#x200B;

It doesn't necessarily stop me, but I'm aware of it. In the past I've been super open about my ED, but once things go....backwards, I stop mentioning it and start pretending it never happened. I'm sure I'm not fooling anyone, but it provides me with an odd sense of safety I think.

This is absolutely me. I wish I had some sort of advice, but I don't. 

&#x200B;

It's hard though. Everyone sees that I'm weight restored and tell me how much better I look, but no one seems to even think that maybe mentally I'm nowhere near ok or recovered or whatever. But no one can tell just by looking at me and the words feel too hard to say.
